to make, but I had to.

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:24.750
I couldn't, I couldn't have
them runnin' in the streets

00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:26.060
with me.

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:29.120
I couldn't have them
here. There. Everywhere.

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:32.513
So, as a mother, I had
to make that decision,

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:37.760
and I felt like it was a good decision.

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:40.130
I mean, it has it's goods and it's bads

00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:42.091
because of course, you know,
you want to be with your kids

00:12:42.091 --> 00:12:46.990
but I know they're well taken care of.

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:48.400
They're so smart.

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:49.722
And my dad did a good job with them.

00:12:49.722 --> 00:12:50.690
- [Mark] That's great.

00:12:50.690 --> 00:12:54.013
- So, (sighs) sorry.

00:12:56.184 --> 00:13:00.430
It's a sensitive subject, but yeah.

00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:01.263
- [Mark] Do you still have contact

00:13:01.263 --> 00:13:02.530
with the rest of your family?

00:13:02.530 --> 00:13:03.363
- Um,

00:13:08.980 --> 00:13:11.763
I felt like, I don't have a family.

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:14.893
I feel like I'm by myself.

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:19.522
That kind of plays a part in my kids.

00:13:19.522 --> 00:13:21.263
That's why I had kids.

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:25.123
Because, I wanted to start my own family,

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:30.633
but being so wrapped up
in that lifestyle, I just,

00:13:32.260 --> 00:13:36.700
I couldn't. And the family
that I do have, we don't talk.

00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:38.020
We don't communicate.

00:13:38.020 --> 00:13:40.731
We don't, I'm literally by myself.

00:13:40.731 --> 00:13:43.600
(inhales sharply)

00:13:43.600 --> 00:13:44.433
Um,

00:13:46.256 --> 00:13:48.183
my dad's side of the family,

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:51.880
I don't talk to them at all.

00:13:51.880 --> 00:13:54.230
My mom's side of the
family, I don't know them.

00:13:55.400 --> 00:13:59.490
I saw dad's family kinda when I got older

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:04.713
and got so wild, it was just like,

00:14:06.020 --> 00:14:08.370
they really don't have
that much to do with me.

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:12.213
So, it's like, I'm really
out here by myself.

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:19.440
And I feel like that's why
I am the way that I am.

00:14:19.440 --> 00:14:21.560
I don't let people in.

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:22.393
I don't.

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:26.570
I have a tough skin.

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:28.150
But.

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:29.630
I have friends that, you know,

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:30.750
I've been friends with for a long time.

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:32.473
I consider them my family.

00:14:33.530 --> 00:14:34.363
But,

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:38.470
family, I don't have no family.
I don't know what family is.

00:14:42.517 --> 00:14:43.350
Yeah.

00:14:44.870 --> 00:14:45.910
- [Mark] Do you see your kids, like,

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:47.810
on holidays and things like that?

00:14:47.810 --> 00:14:49.710
- Um, yes.

00:14:49.710 --> 00:14:51.010
I do.

00:14:51.010 --> 00:14:52.077
Like I said, they know who I am.

00:14:52.077 --> 00:14:55.792
You know, you know, I'm Mom.
They're still kinda young.

00:14:55.792 --> 00:14:58.993
They don't know, like, why
isn't Mom with us every day?

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:04.830
But, when they get older, you
know, I'll explain to them.

00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:06.693
And hopefully they understand.

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:10.430
Because, what I didn't want,

00:15:10.430 --> 00:15:13.063
was for my kids to feel how I felt.

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:17.640
But, it was a little
different, because I was

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:22.600
in the home with my mom, but
I still didn't get that love.

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:26.713
I still didn't get, my mom
didn't teach me anything.

00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:32.860
I learned everything on my
own. Periods. To having sex.

00:15:32.860 --> 00:15:35.690
That's probably why I went so crazy.

00:15:35.690 --> 00:15:37.340
'Cause I didn't know what was right.

00:15:37.340 --> 00:15:39.173
I didn't know what was wrong.

00:15:40.027 --> 00:15:41.320
- [Mark] What, what do you wish

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:42.510
was different about your childhood

00:15:42.510 --> 00:15:45.380
that might've changed the
direction of your life?

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:49.373
- Um, I would say the love. Because,

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:53.550
I turned to the streets for the love,

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:54.890
'cause I wasn't getting it at home.

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:57.023
So, I wanted to go get it from somewhere.

00:15:57.900 --> 00:16:02.900
So, I felt like, if I
had that in-home love,

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:05.903
I really don't feel like I
would have turned out how I did.

00:16:11.050 --> 00:16:14.660
Yeah, I wish that would
have been differently,

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:15.493
but it's like,

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:19.460
I felt like I wouldn't be who I am

00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:21.560
without going through what I went through.

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:23.873
But I would,

00:16:25.430 --> 00:16:27.950
I would have hoped that
it went differently.

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:32.240
- [Mark] And when you say you,
a stripper needs to indulge

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:34.453
in something in order to
just do the work, what

00:16:34.453 --> 00:16:36.193
what drug do you typically go to?

00:16:37.091 --> 00:16:42.050
- Um, well, I don't really do drugs.

00:16:42.050 --> 00:16:44.240
I was doing ecstasy pills, though.

00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:46.610
I turned, I had my stage of that

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:48.690
and I had a really bad episode with that.

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:50.083
So, I stopped doing that.

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:54.110
So then I just turned to alcohol.

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:55.740
I would get drunk.

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:56.893
I wouldn't care.

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:00.930
Black out, fall out.

00:17:00.930 --> 00:17:03.003
I didn't care. That was my go-to.

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:07.850
Now, I don't really drink as much

00:17:07.850 --> 00:17:11.290
because of my situations and my episodes.

00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:13.994
But, yeah, my drug of
choice was ecstasy pills

00:17:13.994 --> 00:17:16.810
and I had a really bad
experience with that.

00:17:16.810 --> 00:17:19.750
So, I just stopped.
But I've never done, you know

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:20.693
any other drug.

00:17:21.860 --> 00:17:24.230
But ecstasy pills are addicting as well.

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:25.580
'Cause I was addicted to it.

00:17:25.580 --> 00:17:27.850
Like, I would crave for them.

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:30.550
I would go through the
withdrawals of not having them.

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:32.993
And then, yeah.

00:17:32.993 --> 00:17:35.950
I took a ecstasy pill that I
thought was an ecstasy pill,

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:37.190
and it was something else.

00:17:37.190 --> 00:17:39.110
It was just, it was bad.

00:17:39.110 --> 00:17:40.143
So, I just stopped.

00:17:42.728 --> 00:17:44.390
I'm always around it, though.

00:17:44.390 --> 00:17:46.880
I'm always around drugs.

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:49.690
I just chose not to do drugs

00:17:49.690 --> 00:17:52.653
because of what I've seen growing up,

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:55.040
um,

00:17:55.040 --> 00:17:57.750
you know, with the drugs,
my mom doing drugs.

00:17:57.750 --> 00:18:01.683
So, I didn't, that was never me.

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:06.150
So then when I did try
to give a drug a chance

00:18:06.150 --> 00:18:07.190
it went all bad.

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:09.193
So, just, okay. No.

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:11.063
Yeah.

00:18:11.063 --> 00:18:12.510
So, I turned to drinking.

00:18:12.510 --> 00:18:15.120
I can say that I was like, an alcoholic

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:17.853
for maybe two to three years.

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:21.680
And then, I was like this,

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:26.230
because I, I don't like the feeling of

00:18:27.260 --> 00:18:29.110
something taking over my body.

00:18:29.110 --> 00:18:31.200
And me not being able to control it,

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:33.830
or me being able to, I
don't like that feeling.

00:18:33.830 --> 00:18:34.663
So, it was like,

00:18:34.663 --> 00:18:38.623
I had to get myself together,
'cause I was losing myself.

00:18:39.670 --> 00:18:42.640
And then, I fell into that.

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:44.150
I did that depression mode.

00:18:44.150 --> 00:18:45.520
'Cause it goes back to what I was saying,

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:48.993
like, it runs, like, it's hereditary and,

00:18:51.070 --> 00:18:52.760
I tried to commit suicide.

00:18:52.760 --> 00:18:55.000
So that was like, after I did that

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:58.010
I tried to block everything out.

00:18:58.010 --> 00:18:59.450
So I don't really drink anymore.

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:01.700
I don't pop, like, I don't do.

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:03.640
- [Mark] When did you
try to commit suicide?

00:19:03.640 --> 00:19:06.937
- Um, The end of last year.

00:19:06.937 --> 00:19:08.930
- [Mark] And how did you try?

00:19:08.930 --> 00:19:10.760
- I took pills and

00:19:14.870 --> 00:19:16.500
somebody walked in.

00:19:16.500 --> 00:19:19.030
I want to say, I guess, at the right time.

00:19:19.030 --> 00:19:22.030
And they called the ambulance
and I woke up in the hospital,

00:19:22.030 --> 00:19:24.350
but I was at the point in life,

00:19:24.350 --> 00:19:26.000
I didn't want to be here anymore.

00:19:30.880 --> 00:19:32.430
Oh, Jesus.

00:19:32.430 --> 00:19:34.970
- [Mark] What do you think
keeps you from wanting to

00:19:34.970 --> 00:19:37.070
just get your life together
just for your kids?

00:19:37.070 --> 00:19:39.160
- Right now? That's
what I'm going through.

00:19:39.160 --> 00:19:41.980
I'm going through getting myself together.

00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:45.442
I'm going through trying to
get myself better, because-

00:19:45.442 --> 00:19:47.470
- [Mark] But, but, but I guess
what I'm saying is, people

00:19:47.470 --> 00:19:50.120
will watch this and like,
Oh, that's just an obvious,

00:19:51.010 --> 00:19:52.840
that's obviously the smart decision.

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:54.320
But, but I understand that it's,

00:19:54.320 --> 00:19:55.604
it's much more complex than that.

00:19:55.604 --> 00:19:57.820
- Yeah, I was gonna say,
it's easier said than done.

00:19:57.820 --> 00:19:58.653
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:19:58.653 --> 00:20:00.130
- It's way, way easier.

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:01.940
- [Mark] And I'm trying
to figure out what,

00:20:01.940 --> 00:20:05.360
what it is that is in play that keeps you

00:20:05.360 --> 00:20:07.983
from just being able to
make that simple decision?

00:20:09.400 --> 00:20:13.650
- I want to say, because when
you get used to a lifestyle,

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:16.730
it's hard to just let it go.

00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:19.890
It's been times where
I've tried to, okay, look,

00:20:19.890 --> 00:20:20.800
I'm going to get it together.

00:20:20.800 --> 00:20:22.000
Like, I got to get my kids

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:25.100
and then you fall back
into that lifestyle.

00:20:25.100 --> 00:20:27.605
And then it's just like,
I'm back to square one.

00:20:27.605 --> 00:20:28.623
- [Mark] Do, do you think some of it is

00:20:28.623 --> 00:20:29.590
just your self worth?

00:20:29.590 --> 00:20:33.750
Is, you almost believe you deserve

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:35.280
the treatment that you
get out in the street

00:20:35.280 --> 00:20:37.171
or in the strip club or whatever?

00:20:37.171 --> 00:20:41.283
- I mean, it's maybe,
maybe it's, I'm used to it,

00:20:41.283 --> 00:20:43.360
'cause that's all I know.

00:20:43.360 --> 00:20:44.193
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:20:44.193 --> 00:20:48.040
- But it's like, now it's like, okay

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:52.580
I have to, it's like, it's,
it's, it's not good for me,

00:20:52.580 --> 00:20:57.580
because that lifestyle is
what made me take those pills.

00:20:57.820 --> 00:20:59.960
It made me not want to be here anymore.

00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:01.273
It made me not.

00:21:03.830 --> 00:21:05.890
It was just like, enough was enough.

00:21:05.890 --> 00:21:08.150
And that's why I wanted to kill myself.

00:21:08.150 --> 00:21:10.130
That's why I didn't
want to be here anymore.

00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:10.980
But then it's just like,

00:21:10.980 --> 00:21:12.810
now, I have to look at the situation.

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:13.840
Like, I have people,

00:21:13.840 --> 00:21:16.540
I have little people that look up to me.

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:19.520
So, it's like, I have
to get myself together.

00:21:19.520 --> 00:21:22.233
Um, I've never had a regular job.

00:21:23.740 --> 00:21:25.410
I just got a regular job.

00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:27.630
So it's like, I'm just, I'm trying.

00:21:27.630 --> 00:21:29.220
I just have to keep myself

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:33.030
from falling back into that lifestyle.

00:21:33.030 --> 00:21:34.810
So it's, it's, it's hard.

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:37.060
It's way easier said than done.

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:39.930
But, I have to, because it's like,

00:21:39.930 --> 00:21:41.270
now it's like, I'm getting older.

00:21:41.270 --> 00:21:42.137
I'm not getting younger.

00:21:42.137 --> 00:21:46.440
So, I don't have that much
time. I have to. I have to.

00:21:46.440 --> 00:21:48.130
And then my kids are getting older.

00:21:48.130 --> 00:21:50.020
So, it's like, now they're
going to understand.

00:21:50.020 --> 00:21:51.290
Now they're gonna know, now they're

00:21:51.290 --> 00:21:53.163
gonna see their mom.

00:21:54.541 --> 00:21:57.520
No, like, I don't,
that's what I don't want.

00:21:57.520 --> 00:22:00.750
That's what I fear, because
I know how that feels,

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:01.630
because I went through that

00:22:01.630 --> 00:22:04.626
and I don't want my
kids to go through that.

00:22:04.626 --> 00:22:06.240
- [Mark] Excellent.

00:22:06.240 --> 00:22:07.646
All right, Amber. Thank you
so much for talking to me.

00:22:07.646 --> 00:22:08.910
- Thank you for having me.

00:22:08.910 --> 00:22:09.807
- [Mark] Good luck with
your kids and everything.

00:22:09.807 --> 00:22:11.068
- Thank you.

00:22:11.068 --> 00:22:13.427
- [Mark] Thank you.

00:22:13.427 --> 00:22:15.647
You done had me in here cryin'!

